elvetica,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Yes. Deallocation retain OS configurations, settings. Anything on the permanent disk will remain intact after deallocation. Creating single VM using cyclecloud gui, is just like creating VM using azure portal. It is not a cluster and only give benefit of cyclecloud automation</div><div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></div><div class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)\">2.&nbsp;Does deallocation preserve NVMe data? We understand that NVMe storage is generally ephemeral (volatile), but we noticed that simply rebooting the OS keeps the NVMe data intact.</div><div class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></div><div class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Since this is a temporary storage, data from temporary storage MAY not get preserved after deallocation.</div><div class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></div><div class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)\">3. Could you please let us know which version you tested with? We are currently using version 8.9.0-3754.&nbsp;</div><div class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></div><div class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Today I&nbsp; tested with cyclecloud version 8.9.0-3754, &quot;restart&quot; option using cyclecloud gui is not supported and recommended.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><img id=\"image_0\" width=\"603\" height=\"176\" size=\"98467\" data-outlook-trace=\"F:1|T:1\" src=\"cid:7b556dfb-fe3e-4d76-9bd5-d24a666a88c4\" data-attachment-id=\"84e36866-4080-4a83-b78c-32179800c3a6\" style=\"width:603.837px; height:176px; max-width:1472px\"></div><div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:12pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)\">As far as restart using azure portal, it worked fine for me. The error which you got after restarting using azure portal, will not affect any OS configurations once the VM comes up.<br>Also, restart within OS also worked for me successfully.</div><div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:12pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></div><div id=\"Signature\"><div class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Let me know if any doubt.</div><div class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,sans-serif,serif,EmojiFont; font-size:9pt; color:rgb(36,36,36)\"><span class=\"spanWithBackgroundColor\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Regards,</span></div><div style=\"bac